    "title": "AP News Report: Global Celebrations, Political Developments, and International Events",
    "text": "• Cities worldwide celebrated the new year with fireworks and varying levels of security.\n• Celebrations were more subdued in some areas due to recent events.\n• Former special counsel Jack Smith stated that the January 6th riot would not have happened without President Donald Trump.\n• Chief Justice John Roberts stated that the Constitution remains 'firm and unshaken'.\n• New Orleans increased security for New Year's Day, nearly a year after a truck attack.\n• Zohran Mamdani will become the next mayor of New York City with two swearing-in ceremonies planned.\n• President Donald Trump vetoed two bipartisan natural resources bills.\n• A deep-sea search for Malaysia Airlines Flight 370 has begun in the Indian Ocean.\n• China announced the 'successful completion' of military exercises near Taiwan.\n• Train services through the Channel Tunnel have resumed after power malfunctions, but delays are expected.\n• Thailand released 18 Cambodian prisoners of war as part of a ceasefire agreement.",
